  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Education, crop diversification and food security for Q&apos;eqchi&apos; communities in Fray Bartolom de las Casas, Alta Verapaz</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Asociacin de Mujeres Adelina Caal Maqun (ACM), an organization of Mayan women, will work with residents of 20 Q&apos;eqchi&apos; communities to diversify crops, protect natural resources, develop a more reliable food supply and launch a farmers&apos; market. Forty students will attend ACM&apos;s junior high school where they will study academic subjects as well as agricultural practices that they will teach to ACM&apos;s members. The work will benefit 680 indigenous Q&apos;eqchi&apos; directly and another 300 indirectly.</narrative>
  </description>
